WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.444
(audience claps)
- I love your hair!

00:00:02.444 --> 00:00:07.329
Your hair is so beautiful!
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.329 --> 00:00:10.539
You smell beautiful, you look beautiful--

00:00:10.539 --> 00:00:11.372
- Thank you!

00:00:11.372 --> 00:00:12.661
I just came from work!

00:00:12.661 --> 00:00:14.250
Hi, everybody!
- Oh my gosh!

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.635
- I got dressed in my dressing room.

00:00:15.635 --> 00:00:16.550
(Tichina laughs)
- Oh, you look really,

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.620
that's where you do it, though--

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.820
- Thank you!
- So good job!

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.240
You know each other though, right?

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.487
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Yes.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.483
He and I, we went to Israel together!

00:00:25.636 --> 00:00:26.677
- That's so random!
- We went with this group

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:28.711
called The Creative Coalition.

00:00:28.711 --> 00:00:31.840
It's kind of a bunch of
artists and industry people

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.680
went to Israel, and can I just tell,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.300
the highlight for me was
when we climbed Masada.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.260
- Mount Masada. It was beautiful.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.200
- Is this, you know, ancient fortress,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.160
and one of the big things is that you do

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.790
this really steep, long, hot hike.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:52.080
Everybody was ready, and
everybody had their boots

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.050
and gear, and you know, Tichina comes by

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.560
and she's looking beautiful,

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.995
I'm not exaggerating, wearing heels.

00:00:59.995 --> 00:01:02.993
(Tichina laughs)
Okay, and her bag!

00:01:02.993 --> 00:01:04.090
And a pocketbook.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:05.640
- Just in case we got stranded!

00:01:06.645 --> 00:01:07.970
(audience laughs)
Listen, we can live two weeks

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.530
off the stuff in my pocketbook.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:10.363
(Steven laughs)

00:01:10.363 --> 00:01:11.380
- That's her bug out bag. (laughs)

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.180
- She looked amazing, beautiful,

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.480
this beautiful woman in heels walking up

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.120
this deadly hike to an ancient fortress.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:19.953
That was my favorite memory.

00:01:19.953 --> 00:01:20.786
- I did it, I did it.

00:01:20.786 --> 00:01:22.820
You know what, it was just
such a wonderful experience.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.840
And then even, you know,
getting in the Dead Sea.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:26.673
- Yeah, that's right.

00:01:26.673 --> 00:01:27.731
- [Kelly] I've always wanted to do that!

00:01:27.731 --> 00:01:28.564
- You gotta go.

00:01:28.564 --> 00:01:30.100
I think it should be the
eighth Wonder of the World.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.670
- That's so cool!
- It's really amazing.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:32.725
But we had a good time.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.070
We're buddies.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.260
- You just can't shave before you go

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:36.414
into the Dead Sea.
- Yeah.

00:01:36.414 --> 00:01:38.449
- I'm just gonna, oh that would burn.

00:01:38.449 --> 00:01:39.282
- (Steven) That'd burn.

00:01:39.282 --> 00:01:40.260
- (laughs) Yeah.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.720
I'm just gonna let you know though,

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.150
momma doesn't wear heels unless
I'm being paid, so. (laughs)

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:46.114
- You know what?
- I don't wear heels.

00:01:46.114 --> 00:01:47.761
(audience claps)

00:01:47.761 --> 00:01:49.950
Nope, nope!

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.226
But you are on a classic
sitcom that I loved as well

00:01:53.226 --> 00:01:54.810
♪ Martin ♪

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.643
with Sheneneh,

00:01:55.643 --> 00:01:57.490
I love the whole show. I
thought it was so good.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.440
So what's, other than
people being a fool like me

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.500
and just singing the song
Martin, what do people do?

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.230
They still come up to you
and ask you about that?

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:04.600
- Oh man, they go, "Pam!"

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.149
(everyone laughs)
I don't even answer to my own,

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:08.660
I don't answer to my own name anymore.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.460
- You're like, "My name is not Pam."

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.210
- But you know what's gratifying for me

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.240
is to know that I did a show,

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.550
you know, 28 years ago,
and people still enjoy it.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.340
God has blessed me to
do what I love doing,

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.930
and being on Martin all those years,

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.960
we just really had a good time,

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.080
and for us to see people laugh at it,

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.670
laughter makes the world go round.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.635
It makes the spirit and the soul better.

00:02:32.635 --> 00:02:34.930
(audience claps)
We need to laugh.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:37.363
So I'm happy that people still enjoy it.

00:02:37.363 --> 00:02:38.290
- Yes!

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:41.240
We've literally had all of your costars

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.560
from The Neighborhood on here.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.240
- Yes, and I'm happy I finally made it

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.214
to your damn show!

00:02:45.214 --> 00:02:46.330
(Steven laughs)
- Well, I'm happy you

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.450
finally found time!

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.283
- What!

00:02:48.283 --> 00:02:49.200
(Kelly laughs)
Yes!

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.770
- No, did they speak well of us?

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.910
Were they like, "It's so great!"

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.327
- Beth came back to the
set, and she was like,

00:02:54.327 --> 00:02:56.427
"Oh my god! I love Kelly!

00:02:56.427 --> 00:02:58.510
"Kelly, oh, I had so
much fun on the show!"

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.179
Yeah, she loved it. They all did.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:01.720
Everybody leaves here--
- You know, she introduced me

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.890
to Marie Kondo, and then
Marie Kondo came on the show,

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:04.983
and we had her back.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.530
Do you know Marie Kondo?

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.690
- Beth is in love with her.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:09.523
Beth loves her.

00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:11.100
- I thought Beth was nuts,

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.647
'cause just that part, 'cause I was like,

00:03:12.647 --> 00:03:13.540
"What is this Marie Kondo thing?"

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.520
I had never heard of it.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.203
I am obsessed!

00:03:16.203 --> 00:03:18.740
- I'm a little OCD too, so it works.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.590
Like, organizing,

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.770
ever since I had my daughter,
which was 15 years ago,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.718
I'm still trying to organize my life.

00:03:25.718 --> 00:03:27.740
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.800
Seriously.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.190
Children, they change your life forever

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:34.080
in a good way but in also other ways.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.020
- Yeah, sometimes just tornadoes--

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.361
- Yeah! (laughs)

00:03:37.361 --> 00:03:40.020
- So Cedric told me
about his neighborhood,

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.230
so what was yours like growing up?

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.240
- Oh god, you know I was born and raised

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.073
in Jamaica, Queens.

00:03:44.073 --> 00:03:45.126
- Queens!
- Yeah!

00:03:45.126 --> 00:03:46.793
- Both of you are Queens, that's right!

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.630
(audience cheers)

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.340
- Queens has a lot of great people,

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.340
lotta talented people, but
I lived in a small, like,

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:55.460
I couldn't go past a one block radius.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.007
Everything was according to your block,

00:03:58.007 --> 00:03:59.870
"What block did you live on?"

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.550
And so when rap came out, we were able

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.500
to hear rap songs from the
Bronx and Brooklyn so you knew,

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.930
that's what rap was about.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.616
But being from Queens
during the '90s and the '80s

00:04:11.616 --> 00:04:13.370
it was a good neighborhood.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.060
I was a little kid, I would
walk in people's doors,

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.090
everybody left the door unlocked--

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:18.923
- Oh no!
- And we'd watch

00:04:18.923 --> 00:04:19.860
each other's kids,

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.103
but it's a little (laughs)--

00:04:21.103 --> 00:04:22.662
- Nope!

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.030
- But it's a very blue-collar burrow

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.980
with amazing diversity.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.330
It was never the coolest burrow,

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.540
but now it's got a best food,

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.470
it's got an amazing
neighborhood, so it's--

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.740
- I always tell people,
whenever you land at JFK,

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.860
I lived like, seven blocks from JFK.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.310
I remember the big planes
would come in at night,

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.950
the Concord would come in
really, really, really--

00:04:42.950 --> 00:04:43.990
- Windows rattle.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.860
- My whole house would shake.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.593
- We had a train behind us, yeah.

00:04:47.593 --> 00:04:49.210
- Same thing!

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.700
I think we all have similar neighborhoods,

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.950
in a way, where it is about community.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:55.783
- Yeah!

00:04:55.783 --> 00:04:57.590
- A neighborhood is
always about community,

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.270
and even if you don't know someone,

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.210
like, I try to make a difference

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.090
by not being shut off from people,

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.457
and if I get new neighbors I'm like,

00:05:04.457 --> 00:05:06.037
"Hey, how you doing?"

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:09.260
- Trying not to be fearful of
something you may not know.

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:10.540
- I'm not fearful, I just wanna make sure

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:11.823
they ain't trying to steal my stuff.

00:05:11.823 --> 00:05:14.159
(everyone laughs)

00:05:14.159 --> 00:05:15.495
(audience claps)
- I'm just introducing myself

00:05:15.495 --> 00:05:17.328
so I know who to find.

00:05:18.215 --> 00:05:19.322
Who to find later.

00:05:19.322 --> 00:05:20.436
I wanna see your face!

00:05:20.436 --> 00:05:22.650
- I need to see who's
gonna be in this house!

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:23.890
- It's harder to steal from someone

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.080
when you're looking 'em in the eyes!

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.870
- Early identification program.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:28.470
(Tichina and Kelly laugh)

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.070
- That was the first round, yes.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:32.378
So your daughter is almost 16.

00:05:32.378 --> 00:05:33.820
What's she like?

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.490
We have a three, five,
13, and 18 year old.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:39.103
- I mean, you lost me
after the second one.

00:05:40.301 --> 00:05:41.390
- No, but a teenager!

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:42.223
That can be trying.

00:05:42.223 --> 00:05:44.680
- Oh my god, just keep us in your prayers.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.240
My daughter,
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.530
it's hard to watch herself.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.630
She's like, now that she's
older it's like watching myself.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.470
It's scary.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:56.200
But what I'm so grateful to
God for is that I am a woman

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.953
and I can teach her how to be a woman.

00:05:57.953 --> 00:05:59.970
(audience claps)
Had I had a male child,

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.670
it would've been a little different.

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:05.560
I was a single mom, which
I did not expect to be,

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.970
I didn't have her until
I was 35 years old,

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.200
so had already had career first,

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:14.130
and then kinda, you know,
got into motherhood.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.020
I think it's been the most gratifying,

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.550
amazing, and just rocky road

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.280
that I've ever taken in my life,

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:23.810
but she's that one person that I would die

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:25.456
in the blink of an eye for.

00:06:25.456 --> 00:06:29.475
So it's motherhood first
and then everything else.

00:06:29.475 --> 00:06:31.525
(audience claps)
- There's so much love,

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.590
and then sometimes there's
so much dislike. (laughs)

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:36.450
- No!

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:37.730
- [Kelly] There's so much love, but yeah,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:38.902
sometimes I'm like--

00:06:38.902 --> 00:06:39.735
- You've got four--

00:06:39.735 --> 00:06:41.207
- "I love you, but I
don't like you right now,

00:06:41.207 --> 00:06:45.260
"so for your safety you should
leave my presence." (laughs)

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.130
- That's because they didn't know us

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.110
before we were moms!

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:51.384
I keep telling her, I was like, "Yo!

00:06:51.384 --> 00:06:52.418
(Kelly laughs)

00:06:52.418 --> 00:06:55.818
"I used to be somebody
before I was your mother!

00:06:55.818 --> 00:06:59.061
"And you might be meeting
this person real soon!"

00:06:59.061 --> 00:07:00.860
(audience laughs and claps)

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:01.693
- And you--

00:07:02.813 --> 00:07:04.887
- "Do you wanna meet that person?"

00:07:04.887 --> 00:07:06.724
- All right, take it easy.

00:07:06.724 --> 00:07:07.557
Take it easy there.

00:07:07.557 --> 00:07:09.527
- And it's like, "And
apologize for what you did

00:07:09.527 --> 00:07:12.034
"to my body. That's all I want."

00:07:12.034 --> 00:07:12.867
- It's too good.

00:07:12.867 --> 00:07:13.770
I give it up to mothers.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:15.730
God bless you. I think it's wonderful--

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:16.630
- I love being a mother.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:17.670
I never thought I'd be one.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.047
My mom is still like, "Oh my god,

00:07:19.047 --> 00:07:20.325
"you have children and a husband."

00:07:20.325 --> 00:07:21.655
- Hey, ain't no problem. (laughs)

00:07:21.655 --> 00:07:23.640
- But Tichina, you've got a way,

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:25.440
this is my favorite thing I've ever heard

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:26.450
with parenting,

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:28.190
you've got a way with your daughter

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.210
to kind of punish her, and
it deals with a cell phone.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:33.290
- Oh, most definitely.

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:37.870
We live in a day and age
where we all have cell phones.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.860
We are attached to our devices,

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.100
and you know, I tried
taking the cell phone

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.730
away from her, which it
wasn't really advantageous

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.020
for me because she takes Uber sometimes,

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.700
and we need the cell phone.

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.661
So, "Okay, Imma get you a flip phone."

00:07:53.661 --> 00:07:55.430
- Ooh, wait a minute.
- I got a flip phone,

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:58.560
and now everything goes
through my phone, so I know how

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.380
to shut her down when I need to.

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.590
There's a way of punishing someone

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:05.330
without not having contact with them.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:06.390
We can still have contact,

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:07.690
but I had to give her a flip phone

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.620
because it's all the control I have.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.370
- When she's with her friends

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:13.350
and she pulls out her
Ferris Bueller phone--

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.530
- Yeah! Oh yeah!

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.954
Take it back to the old days.

00:08:16.954 --> 00:08:18.263
That's when mommy had a flip phone,

00:08:18.263 --> 00:08:20.350
you can have a flip phone, too!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:21.732
- Give her a beeper!
(audience claps)

00:08:21.732 --> 00:08:22.565
(everyone laughs)
I love you!

00:08:23.441 --> 00:08:24.274
Oh my god!

